    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0137" n="53" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg53"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/3355</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 4, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: There is forwarded herewith a paraphrase
                    of a cablegram dated March 1, 1918, from Vice Admiral Sims, U. S. Navy, giving the substance of a letter
                    received by him from the British Admiralty in regard to the disposition of
                    prisoners of war captured by United States naval forces in European waters.</p>
                <pb facs="0138" n="54" xml:id="pg54"/>
                <p>I have the honor to request the opinion of the Department of State on the subject
                    matter, in order that early action may be taken by the Navy and War
                    Departments.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d82-a1.xml" xpointer="d82-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
